FIX-DESKTOP-LIB-ROT-001 — classification of the 37 flagged lts-desktop lib failures (board t_765fb6ab)
HEAD under verification: 56ee3e8 (tree clean; code content identical to 3251b04 for Rust sources)

== Verdict ==
ZERO real rot. The flagged 37-failure set is ENVIRONMENT NOISE: it was measured in a scratch
worktree, where the gitignored bundle media (languages/*/media/*.wav, 4,935 ja-JP files) is
absent, and the pack-archive builders deliberately refuse to bake a pack whose declared media
is missing (ADR-0016 / ADR-0024). In any tree that has the media (the main working tree, or CI
after the "Restore reference-pack audio (published archives)" step), the FULL lib suite is green.
No engine, validator, or test change was needed or made — this card ships evidence only.

== Gate runs (this card, unpiped exit codes recorded inside the logs) ==
1) cargo test -p lts-desktop --lib   — MAIN TREE @ 56ee3e8:
   test result: ok. 207 passed; 0 failed; 2 ignored — exit 0
   Full output: test-main-tree-HEAD.log (201s wall; media present: 4,935 wavs on disk)
2) cargo test -p lts-desktop --lib   — CLEAN SCRATCH WORKTREE at the SAME HEAD
   (git worktree add scratch/lts-desktoplibrot 56ee3e8, shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR; media wavs = 2):
   test result: FAILED. 169 passed; 38 failed; 2 ignored — failure names in worktree-failures.txt

== Failure-set reconciliation ==
Flagged run (FIX-READER-FLOW-001b-1, worktree lts-fixreader001b1, 7ba4df0 era): 167 passed / 37 FAILED,
finished in 21.70s. This card's worktree run: 169 passed / 38 FAILED, finished in 21.88s.
Same family, same near-instant runtime (pack-load refusals fail fast, unlike the 201s media-present
run), one extra failure because the suite grew since (new tests from 3251b04 etc. join the same
media-dependent family). The upstream evidence never recorded the 37 NAMES (process gap); the
worktree reconstruction above reproduces the family exactly.

== Per-failure classification (all 38) ==
- 35 x panic: "no generated audio is present, so this archive could only ship a silent pack:
  run scripts/generate-pack-audio.py first (ADR-0016; the on-demand synthesis fallback this
  used to tolerate was removed by ADR-0024)" — archive bake refuses a silent pack.
- 2 x panic: "pack has 4935 validation error(s); ... media/ja.contrast.gemination.kite-0.wav is
  declared by the media manifest and absent while other declared assets are present: the media
  build is partial" — the 4935 count == exactly the wavs missing in the worktree.
- 1 x dictation_check_matches_spoken_target: engine-error assertion, downstream of the same
  unavailable pack.
Family names match the upstream description ("ja-pack/plan/provenance/pronunciation tests"):
bundled_japanese_pack_installs_and_records, provenance_payload_covers_every_installed_pack_verbatim,
pronunciation_demo_comes_from_pack_contrasts, a_fresh_ja_jp_plan_is_all_introductions..., goal_map_*,
plan_generation_stays_fast_on_the_reference_pack, etc. (full list: worktree-failures.txt).

== Why this is noise, not a defect ==
The media-missing refusal is BY DESIGN (silent packs are a shipped-quality hazard; ADR-0024
removed the fallback that used to tolerate it). CI restores the wavs from the published archives
pinned in catalog/packs.json before running these targets. A git worktree without that restore
step is not a supported environment for the bundled-pack fixtures.

== Honest CI/agent expectation going forward ==
- `cargo test -p lts-desktop --lib` is green ONLY where the 4,935 ja-JP (+ ru-RU) wavs are on disk:
  the main working tree or CI after the media-restore step. In a bare worktree expect exactly this
  ~38-test family red — compare failure SETS, never counts (per lts-concurrent-lane-commits).
- Future cards must record the failing test NAMES in gates.log, not only the count (the gap that
  forced this reconstruction).
